\p{2026-11-24, 13:20Z - 15:15Z. Reviewed: \code{\verb~|rlvm-machine~} as published at 12:47Z (jar \code{\verb~|608b84b2b142~}, the integrator's final state: distribution copy \code{\verb~|work/soundness/dist~}, every run "through the launcher" below), and again in-process against the main tree as published until 15:05Z (after M4's fix of S-F1 / S-F2 at 14:30Z and M6's fix of S-F4 at 14:46Z). Ground truth everywhere: the official checker (\code{\verb~|leanchecker --from-export~}, Lean 4.36.0, through \code{\verb~|rlvm-testkit/bin/testkit verdict~}), never the reference engine alone.}

\p{"Wrong ACCEPT" below means: the process accepts an export that the official checker rejects (owner note 11: resemble official). By my analysis all five findings accept statements that are true in the declarative theory (proof irrelevance plus congruence; a complete level relation); I found no export on which the machine proves \code{\verb~|False~}. They are verdicts the official checker does not give, which is what the arena scores.}

\subtree{
\title{1. Verdict}

\p{Five findings; four were wrong ACCEPTs of the machine as published at 12:47Z, one of them in v0. All four were fixed by their owners during the review and the fixes are verified below; the fifth (universe levels) is the known project-wide difference and is still open.}

\p{State of the main tree as published by 15:16Z (machine: M4 14:30Z, M6 14:46Z / 15:07Z, M5 15:01Z, M7 15:10Z):}

\table{
\tr{\th{Configuration}\th{Verdict}\th{Why}}
\tr{\td{\strong{v0 (no switch)}}\td{no open finding of the machine itself; \strong{S-F3 (levels) open}}\td{S-F5 (wrong ACCEPT in v0: canonical free variables + pair table + eager reduction) is closed by M6's rule M6-F26: a declaration that enters eager reduction is DECLINED by the machine and checked by the reference engine (0.30 \% of Init's, 0.20 \% of Std's declarations apply \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~}). 329 hostile exports: official verdict or a decline by design}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} (candidate default of step 1)}\td{no open finding of its own; inherits S-F3}\td{S-F4 (POS pairs survived a declaration) is closed by the same rule. \code{\verb~|gated~} and \code{\verb~|expect~} had no finding at any time}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|probes~}}\td{no open finding; what is left is order-only}\td{S-F1: B1 / B12 / B2 answered T by congruence where the official procedure is not a congruence. M4 removed them from every switch set (pass B, quick refutation, UNDEC, debt remain)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|facts~}}\td{no open finding; what is left in conversion is B7}\td{S-F2: B3 / B4 / the Prop mask of structure eta skipped positions the official procedure compares and fails on. Removed from every switch set}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|tele~}, \code{\verb~|code~}, \code{\verb~|casetrees~} (K1 roles), \code{\verb~|inert~}}\td{no finding at any time}\td{61 exports built to pass the rent-to-own threshold (and \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.elabAt=1~} through the launcher): case trees on Nat literals / offsets / families / enumerations, CASESON, leaves, over-application, TELE domain patterns with levels and closures. Shape recognition is structural, never by name}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|lazyeval~} (new, 14:00Z)}\td{no finding in the matrix (section 5); argument in 4.3}\td{order-only by construction; reviewed lightly}}
