}

\p{\strong{Which switch sets are safe to be on by default.} On the evidence of this review (section 5) and with the fixes above: \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} gives the official verdict wherever v0 does; I have no objection to it as the default once (1) S-F3 is closed (it is a wrong ACCEPT of both engines today) and (2) the differential gates on the four corpora and the mutant corpora have been re-run on the fixed tree - I did not run them, and M4's, M6's, M5's and M7's publications of 14:30Z - 15:10Z changed behaviour (among other things nearly every declaration that applies \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~} now goes to the reference engine: expect about 164 declines on Init and 203 on Std, by design; a gate that reads \code{\verb~|machine.declined == 0~} must subtract \code{\verb~|machine.eagerDeclines~}). \code{\verb~|probes~}, \code{\verb~|facts~}, \code{\verb~|lazyeval~} and the K1 roles show no finding as published now, but two of them were unsound four hours into a wave that had measured them "clean on everything": I would keep them opt-in until their owners' NOTES state the argument for what is left and the gates are green on the fixed tree. Nothing in this review argues against v0.}

\p{What the four fixed findings have in common: the machine answered from something that is true declaratively (congruence; a pair accepted in another scope or mode), and the official \code{\verb~|is_def_eq~} is neither a congruence, nor transitive, nor a function of the pair alone. Every future shortcut needs the question "does the OFFICIAL procedure give this answer here", not "is this answer true".}
}

