\subtree{
\title{6. Not done, not verified}

\ul{
\li{The four large corpora were not re-run by me (no behaviour of the machine was changed by package S); the integrator's and M4's gates stand for them.}
\li{Native image: every run of mine is the JVM launcher or in-process.}
\li{Parallel workers: one switch set of batch 1 ran with four workers (clean); no hostile export targets the scheduler, publication of facts or code under contention.}
\li{Speculative segments: no export forces a cut (budget exhaustion inside a TRY) on purpose; the review of \code{\verb~|Frames.k_try~} and of what is written before a cut is by reading.}
\li{K2 / T2 are off and were not reviewed. \code{\verb~|pchk~} has no code. The experiment switches \code{\verb~|m1a .. m7b~}, \code{\verb~|t2~} registered at 14:00Z were not reviewed.}
\li{\code{\verb~|Nat.gcd~}, bitwise operations, shifts and \code{\verb~|log2~} are not in \code{\verb~|init-prelude~}; no hostile export covers them.}
\li{A second mode switch of the official kernel was looked for and not found (definition safety and the local context do not change an answer for a pair); if one exists, S-F5 has a sibling.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{7. Addendum of the wave-6 integrator (2026-11-24, 18:15Z - 19:40Z; not part of package S's review)}

\p{State of the findings on the main tree of 19:10Z (machine jar \code{\verb~|78c74ca92785~}, reference jar \code{\verb~|ca1f9bd918bb~}):}

\table{
\tr{\th{Id}\th{State}\th{Evidence}}
\tr{\td{S-F1, S-F2}\td{fixed (M4, 14:30Z); the removed shortcuts are reachable only through \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.m4=congruence,skipargs~}, never through a switch set}\td{the 16 rows pass under all 32 switch sets below}}
\tr{\td{S-F4, S-F5}\td{closed by the decline rule (a declaration that enters eager reduction is declined; the reference engine decides)}\td{the 5 rows and the 11 \code{\verb~|eager-decline~} rows under all 32 sets; the rule declines 164 / 203 / 6,711 declarations of Init / Std / mathlib (statistic \code{\verb~|machine.eagerDeclines~})}}
\tr{\td{\strong{S-F3}}\td{\strong{closed}: both engines compare universe levels as the official kernel does by default (\code{\verb~|Levels~} of the machine since 14:22Z, rlvm-ref \code{\verb~|ca1f9bd918bb~} since 16:03Z); \code{\verb~|levels-complete~} / \code{\verb~|-X levels=complete~} is the opt-in}\td{\code{\verb~|arena-imax-right-successor~}, \code{\verb~|arena-imax-nested-absorption~} are REJECTED under every set; the strict test \code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest#noKnownFindingIsLeft~} passes and the mark \code{\verb~|levels~} is gone from \code{\verb~|s/manifest.tsv~}}}
}

\p{The matrix was run again with the switches that did not exist or had no name when the review ended (\code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~}, in-process, the manifest's official verdicts): 32 switch sets x 329 exports = 10,528 judgments, \strong{0 unexpected verdicts, 0 known findings that still reproduce}. The 15 new sets: \code{\verb~|bodies~}, \code{\verb~|same~}, \code{\verb~|match~}, \code{\verb~|joint~}, \code{\verb~|pchk~}, \code{\verb~|directrules~}, \code{\verb~|code,casetrees,lazycases~}, \code{\verb~|k2,directrules~}; step 1 with \code{\verb~|bodies~}, with \code{\verb~|same~}, with \code{\verb~|match,joint,pchk~}; the new default set (\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,bodies,pchk,match,joint,code,casetrees,lazycases,directrules,lazyeval,same~}) with and without \code{\verb~|same~} and with \code{\verb~|k2~}; \code{\verb~|all~} plus every new switch.}

\p{What this does NOT replace: an adversarial review of the new switches. Section 6 lists \code{\verb~|pchk~}, the experiment switches and K2 as not reviewed, and \code{\verb~|same~} (M4's request of 15:26Z) was never attacked by package S. They are in the default set on the strength of the matrix above, M8's gate (differential, tier equivalence, convention equivalence, the audits \code{\verb~|memocheck~} and \code{\verb~|shortcheck~}, which re-derive every answer of \code{\verb~|same~} and of PCHK by the complete procedure, on all 230 tests and the four corpora), 17,775 mutants and the DiffEngine runs on six corpora ([design-switches-document](design-switches-document)). The general lesson of section 1 applies to each of them: the question is whether the OFFICIAL procedure gives the answer, not whether the answer is true. For \code{\verb~|same~} the argument is that it answers T only for two values that read back to the same expression up to beta, zeta and literal canonicalisation - the condition under which value identity (v0) is the official answer; for PCHK that a closed, level-parameter-free term that passed check mode once has the same type everywhere its declarations are visible, and the bit is never set after an eager-reduction comparison. A next review should attack both, and \code{\verb~|bodies~} / \code{\verb~|match~} / \code{\verb~|joint~} / \code{\verb~|lazycases~} / \code{\verb~|directrules~}, with exports of its own.}

\p{\strong{21:00Z, after this addendum was written: FIVE NEW FINDINGS (E1-F1 .. E1-F5), wrong ACCEPTs, three of them in v0.} Agent E1 wrote hostile exports of a shape neither package S nor this addendum had (\code{\verb~|work/e1/exports/~}, 67 exports with the official verdicts): over package S's non-transitive triple (\code{\verb~|d intro = d h~} and \code{\verb~|d intro = 5~} accepted officially, \code{\verb~|d h = 5~} rejected) a bound variable must have the binder's DECLARED type, and the machine gives it a type that is merely convertible with it: the type inferred for a let VALUE (F1), for the ARGUMENT of a beta redex whose codomain is re-inferred in ONLY mode (F2), the other side's domain when a lambda is compared with a Pi behind a first binder (F3); with \code{\verb~|expect~} the comparison variable carries the lambda's own domain (F4) and the expected codomain is stored as the lambda's (F5). The matrix above did not contain such a row, and the corpus gates compare with the reference engine on terms whose types coincide. The machine was the default engine from 19:41Z to 20:35Z on the evidence of this addendum and is not any more (\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} = 10) until these are fixed (E1: a gated patch for F1, a design for F2 - F5) and E1's rows are strict rows of \code{\verb~|s/manifest.tsv~}. Section 6's "not reviewed" list was the warning; this addendum should not have been read as a review.}
}
